HST Office: the 1.0.2 ribbon mockup's frame: a 106 px body, the banner 8 px from the window's edge, ⌘⌥R on macOS.

- The ribbon with the banner (Tabbed notebookbar of Writer, Sheets, Slides and Draw) is the tab row, 3 px, a body of
  exactly 106 logical px and 3 px in every tab (35 + 112 = 147 px with the 35 px tab row). It was at least 165 px and
  grew with the tallest page (198 px in Writer at 1920 px); content taller than the body is a .ui to fix. Other
  notebookbar files keep the 165 px minimum.
- slotFor() no longer takes 2 px above and below the slot: in the 106 px body the banner is w x w*104/360, centred
  (360 x 104 at 1920 px, 269 x 78 at 1485, 260 x 75 up to 1440, 390 x 113 at 150 %), instead of 353 x 102. Its width follows the document
  window's frame (windowSlotWidth got the SystemWindow's narrower client: 357 px at 1920), its right edge is 8 px
  from the window's right edge and the groups stop 8 px before it.
- Compact ribbon: the banner is 260 x 75 (compactSlot) centred in the 80 px band, 8 px from the window's edge; the
  tab row, the quick row and the dropped page stop 8 px before it (W - 276 px).
- macOS (owner decision D10): ⌘⌥R switches the compact ribbon as Ctrl+F1 does; Ctrl+F1 also works there.
- File page (mockup reference/mockup-writer-backstage-1366.png): while the panel is open, a title band covers the
  ribbon's body left of the banner: a round back button (closes the panel, as Esc does), the greeting and
  "Tệp tin · <document title>" (the File tab's label and the model's XTitle, no new string). The panel still starts
  below the document tab strip (owner, 14/11/2026) and no longer repeats the greeting; the banner is unchanged. The
  band is a child of the ribbon's tab control, on top of its page, and is disposed before the tab control goes.

